cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Purser in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Purser"
abstract: >-
  A model supply-chain control plane: policy, provenance, and enforcement for
  machine-learning model artifacts. Static malicious-code and
  data-exfiltration scanning is one signal input, alongside verified
  provenance (Ed25519/Sigstore) and upstream scan-verdict ingestion; policy
  (country of origin, publisher, name, format, signer identity) renders a
  verdict enforced in CI and at Kubernetes admission.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The Purser Authors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/purser-io/purser"
url: "https://purser-io.io"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.2.1
date-released: "2026-07-28"
keywords:
  - security
  - machine-learning
  - supply-chain
  - model-scanning
  - mlsecops
